commit b295f8b49773ae61e0ff931d0352fe9fb29612ed
Author: Dex Research <research@dex.local>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 17:04:22 2026 +0100

    fix(inventory): lock SKUs one at a time when settling an order

    commit, release and expire took every SKU lock of a bundle and held the
    first while queuing for the next, so callers of a bundle's other SKUs
    waited behind a busy SKU they do not share. Each SKU's change stands
    alone and the order lock already rules out a second settle, so settle
    now locks one SKU at a time.

    The class doc now says what the locks do and do not promise: a bundle
    reserve still takes its SKUs together to check them all at once, and
    services only exclude each other when given the same store object.

    The keyed-lock tests now catch a lock that forgets a key while a waiter
    is still queued.

    Co-Authored-By: Dex <noreply@dexcode.ai>
