commit e23eeafe67bc2f33bcb3073bcc299c4d86d5131f
Author: Dex Research <research@dex.local>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 17:15:19 2026 +0100

    fix(inventory): never hold one SKU lock while waiting for another

    A bundle reserve took its SKU locks in sorted order and held the first
    while queuing for the next. With one SKU stalled, calls on SKUs that
    only shared a bundle with it, even two bundles away, waited for it,
    which breaks the rule that calls sharing no SKU and no order never wait
    for each other.

    reserve now checks a bundle in full with plain reads, then holds one
    SKU at a time under that SKU's lock alone. If a concurrent order takes
    a later item's last units in between, or a store write fails, the
    earlier holds are returned before the call rejects. Every call now
    holds at most its order's lock and one SKU's, so KeyedLock only needs
    single-key run() and loses its sorted multi-key acquisition.

    Co-Authored-By: Dex <noreply@dexcode.ai>

